    <article class="article">
      <p class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</p>
      <h1>50cc Motorbike Hanoi: Students Daily Rental Planning</h1>
      <p>A semester in Hanoi runs on a fixed routine: lectures at one campus, library sessions at another, coffee-shop study groups in the Old Quarter. A small 50cc scooter rented by the day slots into that routine without the long commitment of buying a machine you must resell before flying home. At the shop on 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, open daily from 09:00 to 21:00, the 50cc class rents for 200,000 VND per day, and every one of those days should be a day you actually ride.</p>
      <p>This guide shows how to plan rental days around a student timetable instead of paying for idle ones. For the wider picture of small-displacement bikes in the city, read the <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/">50cc motorbike rental guide for Hanoi</a>, compare full pricing across the fleet on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost page</a>, and check the <a href="/faq/">rental FAQ</a> for the questions students ask most often.</p>
      <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
        <p>What you will find in this guide:</p>
      <ol>
      <li><a href="#sec-1">Why daily rental planning matters for students</a></li>
      <li><a href="#sec-2">Matching rental days to your class timetable</a></li>
      <li><a href="#sec-3">Budgeting the daily rate honestly</a></li>
      <li><a href="#sec-4">Picking up the bike at the shop</a></li>
      <li><a href="#sec-5">Route planning across the city</a></li>
      <li><a href="#sec-6">Weather and seasonal planning</a></li>
